    "content": "The RBC Heritage features a sudden-death playoff if players are tied after 72 holes of stroke play. The playoff begins immediately on the par-4 18th hole at Harbour Town Golf Links, alternating with the par-3 17th hole if necessary until a winner is determined by the lowest score.Key Playoff Details:Format: Sudden-death (first player to win a hole wins the tournament).Holes Used: The playoff starts on the 18th hole and moves to the 17th hole if necessary, repeating this rotation until a winner emerges.Recent History: The 2023 and 2025 events both went to playoffs, with winners Matt Fitzpatrick (2023, 2026) and Jordan Spieth (2022) winning in extra holes.Tournament Context: As a PGA Tour Signature Event, the 70-plus player field plays for 700 FedEx Cup points and no cut is made after 36 holes.The playoff format ensures that tied players continue competing to secure the victory, often utilizing the challenging finishing holes of the Harbour Town course.",
